# Deny-by-default: only file types this project deliberately tracks are
# un-ignored below. Kept as a whitelist because run artifacts (npz, png, large
# json) are numerous and easy to commit by accident.
#
# Extended for the CI/Popperian work (POPPER_PLAN.md): before this pass the
# whitelist was *.py and *.md only, which silently ignored pyproject.toml,
# requirements/*.txt, .github/workflows/*.yml and claims/*.json -- i.e. every
# file CI and the prediction registry need. `git check-ignore -v <path>` is the
# thing to run when a newly added config file mysteriously will not commit.
*
!*.py
!*.md
!.gitignore
!pytest.ini
!*/

# --- config / CI / declarative records -------------------------------------
# NB: gitignore has no inline comments -- a trailing "# ..." becomes part of
# the pattern and silently stops it matching. Keep these bare.
!*.toml
!*.cfg
!*.ini
!*.yml
!*.yaml
!*.sh
!requirements/*.txt

# The prediction registry and its adjudication records are the project's
# falsification ledger, not run output -- they are tracked deliberately.
# Scoped to claims/ so this does not un-ignore result json elsewhere.
!claims/*.json
!claims/**/*.json

# run artifacts
results/
metastability_results/

# python cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
